  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "T.J. Otzelberger is the head men's basketball coach at Iowa State University, holding the position since March 2021. He has led the Cyclones to significant success, including multiple Sweet 16 appearances (2022, 2024) and high-level conference performance, establishing himself as a key figure in the program's recent turnaround. Key Details About T.J. Otzelberger: Tenure: He was hired on March 18, 2021, as the 21st head coach in program history. Performance: As of March 2026, he has led the team to over 90 wins in his first four years, the most in school history for that span, and maintains high winning percentages. Background: Before joining Iowa State, Otzelberger was the head coach at South Dakota State and had previous assistant coaching roles at Iowa State under Greg McDermott, Fred Hoiberg, and Steve Prohm. Style: Known for building strong defensive, high-energy teams and a focus on player development. He is currently leading the Cyclones in the 2026 NCAA Tournament.",
